.TH BOSWAS-CAMERA 1 "November 2026" "Boswas OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boswas-camera \- take photos and record videos with a camera of the computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-camera
.br
.B boswas-camera
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-camera
shows the live picture of a camera and takes photos and videos with it.
Only one instance runs per session; a later start brings the window of the
running one to the front.
It has one window, as Camera has on Windows: a camera delivers its picture
to one program at a time. A start with
.B \-\-new\-window
brings the window forward as well.
.PP
The picture fills the middle of the window.
On the right are the shutter button, the buttons for photo and video mode, a
button to change the camera when more than one is connected, and a small
picture of the last capture, which opens it in
.BR boswas\-photos (1)
(a video, or any capture when Photos is not installed, opens in the default
application).
On the left are the settings, the timer (off, 3, 5 or 10 seconds, counted
down on the picture; the shutter button or Escape cancels it), the mirror
and grid switches and, only when the camera reports the feature, flash, light
(in video mode), exposure, focus and, under the picture, zoom.
.SS Photos
A photo is saved as JPEG in
.IR Pictures "/Camera Roll"
with the time in its name, for example
.BR IMG_20261116_143005.jpg .
Mirroring affects the preview only: the file is the picture as the camera
sees it.
The shutter animation is left out when the desktop asks for reduced motion.
.SS Videos
A video is recorded to
.IR Videos "/Camera Roll"
as
.BR VID_ ...,
in an MPEG-4 file with H.264 and AAC where the system can encode them, with
the sound of the default microphone when there is one (a button turns the
microphone off).
The time recorded so far is shown on the picture; a recording can be paused
and resumed.
Closing the window, or losing the camera, ends the recording and keeps the
file.
.PP
A recording does not start when less than 500 MiB is free where videos are
saved, and a running recording is ended and saved when less than 100 MiB is
left.
A photo needs 20 MiB.
.SS When there is no picture
Without a camera the window says so and starts by itself as soon as one is
connected.
When the camera cannot be started (another program uses it, or access is
not allowed) the message of the system is shown with a button to try again.
When the camera is unplugged, another connected camera takes over; without
one the window waits for the camera to come back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the command line and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Space, Enter|Take a photo; start or stop a recording
Escape|Cancel the timer; leave the settings
Ctrl+,|Settings
Alt+Left|Back to the camera
F5|Look for cameras again
Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q|Close
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/com.boswas.Camera/settings.json
Save locations, the mode and timer to start with, mirror, grid, video
quality, the shutter sound, the camera used last and the resolutions chosen
for each camera.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.Camera/window.ini
The window size.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user\-dirs.dirs
Where the Pictures and Videos folders are (xdg\-user\-dirs).
.TP
.I /usr/share/sounds/freedesktop/stereo/camera\-shutter.oga
The shutter sound, when the sound theme is installed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, also when a running instance was brought to the front;
2 for a wrong command line; 4 when started as root, which is refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-photos (1),
.BR boswas\-media\-player (1),
.BR xdg\-user\-dirs\-update (1)
